HST Office: ribbon groups collapse into their captioned button before anything folds.

As in Office, a group can collapse into one button that shows its caption and an arrow and opens the
group at full size in a popup. The tab's ladder (vcl/inc/HstRibbonLadders.hxx, state 3) says which groups
may do so and when; the chevron popup stays the last rung.

- PriorityMergedHBox: the group buttons sit right after their groups; the ladder measures them as the
  group's last state; a collapsed group is neither a folded group nor part of the chevron popup.
- PriorityHBox: the block beside a merged box (the Home tab's Tools) shows as its button as soon as the
  groups at their full size would not fit beside it, before any group shrinks. The test depends only on
  the width, so the block no longer folds at one width and comes back at a narrower one.
- DropdownBox: such a block's button shows the caption of its group (labelled-by) and an arrow instead
  of a bare menu symbol, and the block keeps the height of its content while collapsed: the tallest tab
  page sets the ribbon's height, so the ribbon no longer changed height (Sheets 182/173 px) depending on
  whether Tools was collapsed at that width.
- The Styles gallery (a group that expands) keeps room for four previews at its large size and two at
  medium, so the ladder narrows it only after Font and Clipboard lost their labels.
- A group collapsed by an earlier step comes back when a later collapse (Paragraph) left room for it.

